      <p class="news-meta">2026 &middot; Accepted by IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing</p>
      <h3 class="news-title"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TMC.2026.3730010">Noncoherent Detection of Constant-Envelope Signals for Mobile Edge Applications &ndash; Asymptotically Optimal Detectors and a Reliability-Based Intelligent Detector</a></h3>
      <p class="news-authors"><b>Mu Jia</b>, <a href="http://chenjunting.org/">Junting Chen</a>, <a href="https://www2.ae-info.org/ae/Member/Liang_Ying-Chang">Ying-Chang Liang</a>, and <a href="https://sai.cuhk.edu.cn/en/teacher/159">Pooi-Yuen Kam</a></p>
      <p class="news-summary">We study how small wireless devices can detect constant-envelope signals using only received magnitudes. The work derives energy and amplitude detectors for different SNR regimes and combines their decisions with an offline-calibrated reliability rule that needs no instantaneous SNR at runtime.</p>
      <p class="news-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TMC.2026.3730010">Paper</a> &middot; <a href="photos/news/tmc-detection-performance.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View figure</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
