    <div class="news-body">
      <p class="news-meta">2026 &middot; IEEE ICC Workshops</p>
      <h3 class="news-title"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/ICCWorkshops63917.2026.11586741">Physics-Aware Tensor Reconstruction for Radio Maps in Pixel-Based Fluid Antenna Systems</a></h3>
      <p class="news-authors"><b>Mu Jia</b>, <a href="https://haosunhs.github.io/index.html">Hao Sun</a>, <a href="http://chenjunting.org/">Junting Chen</a>, and <a href="https://sai.cuhk.edu.cn/en/teacher/159">Pooi-Yuen Kam</a></p>
      <p class="news-summary">We reconstruct radio maps for pixel-based fluid antennas from sparse measurements by combining low-rank tensor structure with antenna physics. The method uses predictable gain differences across antenna modes to recover spatial detail and shadowing boundaries, supporting radio-map-based mode selection.</p>
      <p class="news-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/ICCWorkshops63917.2026.11586741">Paper</a> &middot; <a href="photos/news/icc-radio-map-model.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View figure</a></p>
    </div>
